[10.25, "o", "Claude\r\n"]
[10.55, "o", "  All three fine-tuned a pretrained model on\r\n  each puzzle at test time; they differed in\r\n  what they pretrained and how they decoded.\r\n"]
[10.85, "o", "  Scores below are from the Kaggle\r\n  leaderboard, summaries from each team's\r\n  writeup.\r\n"]
[11.15, "o", "\r\n  1. NVARC (24.03) — [writeup](https://www.kag\r\n  gle.com/competitions/arc-\r\n"]
[11.45, "o", "  prize-2025/writeups/nvarc)\r\n  - Synthetic data: They used an LLM (`gpt-\r\n    oss-120b`) to mix human puzzle\r\n"]
[11.75, "o", "    descriptions into new, harder ones, then\r\n    generate Python programs for the input and\r\n    output grids. After consistency filtering\r\n"]
[12.05, "o", "    this gave about 103k synthetic puzzles.\r\n  - Model: They fully fine-tuned a Qwen3 4B\r\n    model on 3.2M augmented samples, following\r\n"]
[12.35, "o", "    the 2024 ARChitects recipe. At test time\r\n    they applied per-puzzle LoRA fine-tuning,\r\n    a batched depth-first search decoder, and\r\n"]
[12.65, "o", "    augmentation-based rescoring of\r\n    candidates.\r\n  - Tiny Recursive Model: A TRM ensemble was\r\n"]
